# 🧠 LLM from Scratchl

![Transformer Architecture](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400?text=Transformer+Architecture+Diagram)  
*A from-scratch implementation of a Large Language Model (LLM) inspired by [this tutorial](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UU1WVnMk4E8). Designed for educational purposes to demystify modern NLP architectures.*

---

## 🚀 Key Features
- **Tokenization**: Byte-level BPE (Byte Pair Encoding) for text processing.
- **Transformer Core**: Self-attention, multi-head attention, and feed-forward layers.
- **Training Pipeline**: Full workflow from data loading to loss optimization.
- **Lightweight**: Designed for clarity over scalability (runs on CPU/GPU).

---

## 📂 Repository Structure
llm-from-scratch/
├── data/ # Sample training corpus (e.g., TinyShakespeare)
├── tokenizer/ # Custom BPE tokenizer implementation
├── model/ # Transformer architecture (PyTorch)
│ ├── attention.py # Multi-head self-attention
│ ├── blocks.py # Encoder/decoder layers
│ └── transformer.py # Full model
├── train.py # Training script
├── generate.py # Text generation demo
└── config.json # Hyperparameters (vocab size, layers, etc.)

## 📊 Technical Details

    Architecture: Decoder-only transformer (GPT-style).

    Hyperparameters:

        6 layers, 8 attention heads, 512 embedding dim.

        Trained on ~1M tokens (TinyStories or OpenWebText subset).

    Performance: ~2.5 PPL (perplexity) on validation set (varies by dataset).

🤝 Contributing

PRs welcome! Focus areas:

    Optimize training speed (e.g., mixed precision).

    Extend tokenizer (Unicode support).

    Add quantization for lightweight inference.

Built for educational purposes as part of self-study in NLP/LLMs.
